  "type": "numerical",
  "level": 1,
  "question": {
    "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>27</mn></math> identical drops are charged at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>22</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math> each. They combine to form a bigger drop. The potential of the bigger drop will be _____&nbsp;&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math>.",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "198",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/9e5c9397-1c7c-4a9a-858b-152403dee417-e6eae665-9e1f-4be0-868c-2f49ad6d905c-5d4f6ccf-73e4-43b9-996d-09e857a8186f-image.png\" style=\"width: 250px; height: 140px;\" /></p><p>Total volume of the drop will remain unchanged,</p><p>So,&nbsp;&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>27</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mi>&#960;</mi><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mi>&#960;</mi><msup><mi>R</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>r</mi></math></p><p>Potential of the small drops,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>22</mn><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>k</mi><mi>q</mi></mrow><mi>r</mi></mfrac></math></p><p>For bigger drop, potential will be</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>V</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>k</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>27</mn><mi>q</mi></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>r</mi></mrow></mfenced></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>9</mn><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><mi>k</mi><mi>q</mi></mrow><mi>r</mi></mfrac></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>22</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>198</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math></p>",
